+        """E034: evict about ``need_bytes`` of unlocked L1 objects now, in
+        policy order, for a caller whose L1 allocation just failed. The
+        allocator needs one contiguous free block per object, so free bytes
+        can exceed ``need_bytes`` while the allocation still fails
+        (fragmentation); the target is therefore ``need_bytes`` of new free
+        space, independent of the current usage. Called without the L1Manager
+        lock held (L1Manager.delete takes it). At most 3 policy passes, each
+        asking for at most half of the tracked keys.
+
+        Returns:
+            The bytes freed (usage before minus usage after; another thread
+            may change usage in between).
+        """
